Source: obsidian
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), desktop-file-utils, zlib1g, zlib1g-dev
# ^ zlib1g(-dev): the AppImages are EXECUTED at build time
# (--appimage-extract). The arm64 runtime's DT_NEEDED is literally
# `libz.so` (readelf-proven 2026-10-11; the amd64 runtime needs only
# libz.so.1), so the -dev symlink package is required -- the aarch64
# buildroot does not carry it transitively (all 4 deb suites failed
# aarch64 2026-10-11 with `libz.so: cannot open shared object file`;
# zlib1g-dev verified shipping /usr/lib/*/libz.so on Trixie).
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://obsidian.md/

Package: obsidian
Architecture: amd64 arm64
# Wrapper ships x86_64 + arm64 AppImages only (no i386 payload);
# restricting here keeps i586 builders from attempting the build
# (debian/rules has no i386 branch).
# Runtime set: the Electron shell's DT_NEEDED set plus installable
# bundled-helper libs (the get-fonts node module needs fontconfig; tray
# works through the system ayatana stack). NOT included: the bundled
# gtk2-era appindicator helpers' chain (libdbusmenu-gtk.so.4 has no
# installable provider left on Testing, and libgtk2 is being purged) --
# those bundled libs stay dormant while the ayatana path serves the tray.
# t64 names target Debian Testing.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash, hicolor-icon-theme, libasound2t64, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libatspi2.0-0, libayatana-appindicator3-1, libcairo2, libcups2t64, libdbus-1-3, libdbus-glib-1-2, libdbusmenu-glib4, libexpat1, libfontconfig1, libgbm1, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libglib2.0-0t64, libgtk-3-0t64, libnotify4, libnspr4, libnss3, libpango-1.0-0, libsecret-1-0, libudev1, libuuid1, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxkbcommon0, libxrandr2, libxss1, libxtst6, xdg-utils
Description: A powerful knowledge base for plain text Markdown files
 Obsidian is a powerful knowledge base that works on top of a local folder
 of plain text Markdown files.
